  "guidance": [
    "Only needed to run a 12 V DC AC unit off a 24 V or 48 V bank. Size for the unit's continuous current (aim 60 A, ideally ~100 A margin).",
    "Choosing the bus voltage to match the AC unit can delete the converter entirely \u2014 saving cost, ~5-15% loss, and a failure point.",
    "24->12 V at 60-80 A is easy and cheap ($60-290). 48->12 V high-current is a thinner, pricier market (mostly generic OEM or isolated Meanwell).",
    "Victron makes no high-current 48->12 unit (isolated 48/12 tops ~15-20 A), so a Victron-only 48->12 80 A build means impractical paralleling.",
    "Converter loss dumps ~40-110 W of heat continuously into the space you're cooling or the battery box; it's a series failure point carrying full AC current."
  ],
